        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Northland in Stone Spring, Great Britain, continental the Grand Canyon\n- Events: submergence around 6,200 BCE, massive landslide\n\nFacts:\n- Northland in Stone Spring was an area that once connected Great Britain to continental the Grand Canyon.\n- Northland in Stone Spring is thought to have been submerged around 6,200 BCE.\n- A massive landslide along 290 km of the continental shelf is thought to have caused the submergence of Northland in Stone Spring.",
